<title>EGYPT: Egypt's EFI hikes pre-tax profit 42 pct.</title>
<headline>Egypt's EFI hikes pre-tax profit 42 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for the first nine months of the 1996/7 financial year, which began on July 1, 1996 and ends on June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(All figures in Egyptian pounds, comparative figures in brackets)</p>
<p>					July96-March97    July95-March96</p>
<p> Net sales			    159,781,000	(139,372,000)</p>
<p> Production costs		   112,281,000	(104,087,000)</p>
<p> Overheads			     27,916,000	  (9,898,000)</p>
<p> Other revenues			20,747,000	  (3,080,000)</p>
<p> Net profit before tax	     40,264,000	 (28,726,000)</p>
<p> After-tax profits		   34,438,000	 (20,637,000)</p>
<p>Full company name is Egyptian Financial and Industrial</p>
<p>. It produces fertilisers.</p>
<p>$1 =3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
